0); Relationships (13161, 14578)]", "# Public Health Research Community in Spain\n\nThe community encompasses various entities involved in public health research in Spain, focusing on critical health issues such as diabetes, obesity, allergies, and nutritional epidemiology. Key entities include Olveira et al., GEPREM-Hg, FESNAD, and the Society of Allergology and Clinical Immunology, which are interconnected through their research and initiatives aimed at improving health outcomes in the Spanish population.\n\n## Diabetes prevalence as a critical health issue\n\nDiabetes mellitus is a major public health concern in Spain, with a significant number of cases affecting the population. The country ranks fourth in Europe for diabetes prevalence, which poses challenges for healthcare management and resource allocation. Studies such as those conducted by Olveira et al. highlight the importance of enteral nutrition in hospitalized diabetic patients, emphasizing the need for effective nutritional strategies to manage this condition. The interconnectedness of diabetes with other health issues, such as obesity and chronic renal disease, further complicates the public health landscape in Spain [Data: Entities (6423, 580); Relationships (1527, 4113, 4111)].\n\n## Obesity trends among children\n\nThe rising trend of obesity among children in Spain is alarming and has been documented by research groups like Carrascosa et al. This trend is linked to various factors, including dietary habits and lifestyle choices. The implications of childhood obesity extend beyond immediate health concerns, potentially leading to long-term health issues such as diabetes and cardiovascular diseases. The Spanish Federation of Nutrition and Dietetics (FESNAD) plays a crucial role in addressing these issues by promoting healthy dietary practices and guidelines tailored to the Spanish population [Data: Entities (15266, 580); Relationships (4118, 4131)].\n\n## Nutritional guidelines and dietary practices